# Rule-based OHLCV paper simulator with small in-session entry/exit learners;
# it is not a true AI service, durable learner, broker integration, or order system.
# The entry learner only tightens future flat-entry score gates after poor simulated outcomes;
# optional fast mode lowers the flat-entry baseline by one point (floor 2) for more samples.
# Stop/RR, risk sizing, cooldown, full-MTF reversal safeguards and live-order behavior are unchanged.
# Run on a 1-minute chart: completed 1m candles are aggregated into 5m, 15m, 1h, and 4h bars.
# Other chart intervals block entries. Full MTF warmup is about 84 hours; opportunity mode may
# use a confirmed 5m trend after its EMA/ATR are ready, while higher frames warm up. MTF scores
# use completed bars; 1m conditions can change intrabar.
# Higher-timeframe volume is the chart's volume field (possibly tick volume), not trader counts.
# Pending signals are rechecked at the next 1m open. Stop/TP hits use candle ranges; if both
# are touched in one bar, the simulator assumes the stop hit first. In-session entry/exit
# learning state resets when the indicator runtime is reinitialized; it is not durable.
# Equity is optional: without it, trades use one simulated unit and percent risk/drawdown caps
# cannot be calculated. No live orders are placed. Costs are estimates; actual execution differs.
